Negative control for the id-less record that draws at boot (RT3).

A record declaring `drawsEmpty` has no fetch to wait on — the guest affiliate
link visit holds nothing before its first visit — so the surface draws its
header and its controls as soon as the cell is served. This mutant stops
honouring the flag: an empty record reads as a load again, the surface sits on
its skeleton, and the page can never show the Record visit control that would
fill it.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Expected red (component lane): record-surface.spec.ts — a record with
`drawsEmpty` and an empty model must draw its header and footer actions, while
one without it still draws the skeleton.

diff --git a/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/runtime/components/surfaces/RecordSurface.vue b/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/runtime/components/surfaces/RecordSurface.vue
--- a/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/runtime/components/surfaces/RecordSurface.vue
+++ b/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/runtime/components/surfaces/RecordSurface.vue
@@ -501,7 +501,7 @@
 const notice = computed(() => {
   const state = resolveRecordState(meta.value, context.value);
   if (state === ModuleState.UNSERVED) return state;
-  if (props.uischema.drawsEmpty || !isEmpty(record.value)) return undefined;
+  if (!isEmpty(record.value)) return undefined;
   return state === ModuleState.READY ? ModuleState.LOADING : state;
 });

